  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The complete threefold Agnus Dei for Masses for the Dead, reconstructed separately in each 1962 Missal setting from its printed threefold address and explicit replacement rubric. The first two petitions end dona eis requiem; only the third adds sempiternam. No ordinary mercy or peace petition and no breast-striking instruction is carried into this recension. The priestly low-Mass recitation and quiet sung-Mass recitation are distinguished from the sung Ordinary performance (Ritus X.2, X.4 and XIII.1; RG 511 i, 513 e, 514; DMS 25 b, 26, 31 c).",
    "source": {
      "method": "Separately read against the Benziger Editio iuxta typicam and the distinct Vatican setting of the 1962 Roman Missal; the printed clauses and replacement rubrics determine this complete recension. The witness headers and apparatus distinguish source transcription from the rule-derived reading.",
